WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.203 --> 00:00:03.922
(airplane soaring)

00:00:03.922 --> 00:00:06.178
- [Narrator] Find your thing.

00:00:06.178 --> 00:00:07.806
When you're trying to
with the career lottery,

00:00:07.806 --> 00:00:09.418
sometimes the winning ticket is right

00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:10.588
in front of you.

00:00:10.588 --> 00:00:12.639
The answer to your most pressing questions

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:14.951
and the path to the
work you were born to do

00:00:14.951 --> 00:00:18.452
may come from the people
you interact with everyday.

00:00:18.452 --> 00:00:19.837
Everyone's an expert at something,

00:00:19.837 --> 00:00:21.603
is a good principle to keep in mind.

00:00:21.603 --> 00:00:24.407
And often the something
comes as a surprise.

00:00:24.407 --> 00:00:26.633
But even if you know what your skills are,

00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:28.908
a skill is only as valuable as the extent

00:00:28.908 --> 00:00:31.843
to which people will pay you to use it.

00:00:31.843 --> 00:00:33.389
How do you figure out
which our your skills

00:00:33.389 --> 00:00:35.581
are most valuable and marketable?

00:00:35.581 --> 00:00:37.069
Here's the core principle,

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:39.413
when you're not sure what your thing is,

00:00:39.413 --> 00:00:41.186
when you don't know quite where to look

00:00:41.186 --> 00:00:43.057
to find that job or career that brings you

00:00:43.057 --> 00:00:45.046
joy, flow, and a good income

00:00:45.046 --> 00:00:48.188
the people you talk to
everyday can help you find it.

00:00:48.188 --> 00:00:50.192
The answer may come from your inbox,

00:00:50.192 --> 00:00:51.977
whether that inbox consists of the actual

00:00:51.977 --> 00:00:55.649
emails you receive with the
same questions over and over.

00:00:55.649 --> 00:00:57.718
Your social media feeds
are just the conversations

00:00:57.718 --> 00:00:59.177
you have with friends.

00:00:59.177 --> 00:01:01.020
In other words, the people in your network

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.045
may actually have a
better sense of what your

00:01:03.045 --> 00:01:06.179
most marketable skills are than you do.

00:01:06.179 --> 00:01:08.561
The key, is looking to the
questions they ask you.

00:01:08.561 --> 00:01:10.163
The favors they request of you.

00:01:10.163 --> 00:01:12.720
And maybe even the books
or articles they send you,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.381
simply because they think
you'd be interested.

00:01:15.381 --> 00:01:18.280
When someone says hey can
I ask you for a favor?

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.969
And you already know what that
person is going to ask you,

00:01:20.969 --> 00:01:22.761
you have your answer.

00:01:22.761 --> 00:01:24.150
Think about it.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.010
If you have trouble updating your phone,

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:27.403
whom do you ask for help?

00:01:27.403 --> 00:01:28.439
If you've been going to the gym,

00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:30.014
but not seeing results,

00:01:30.014 --> 00:01:32.163
whom do you ask for workout advice?

00:01:32.163 --> 00:01:33.467
When you're planning a trip abroad

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:34.771
and need to find a hotel,

00:01:34.771 --> 00:01:37.315
whom do you ask recommendations?

00:01:37.315 --> 00:01:40.214
Now think about it from
the other perspective.

00:01:40.214 --> 00:01:43.616
Does everyone ask you for
help updating the phone,

00:01:43.616 --> 00:01:45.830
or improving a workout,
or recommending a place

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.748
to stay while traveling.

00:01:47.748 --> 00:01:50.312
If you look closely,
you'll probably find that

00:01:50.312 --> 00:01:52.192
there are certain types
of advice that people

00:01:52.192 --> 00:01:55.000
ask you for over and over.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.763
Whether it's recommendations
for books and movies,

00:01:57.763 --> 00:01:59.589
investing tips, or your thoughts on the

00:01:59.589 --> 00:02:01.532
latest gadget that hit the market,

00:02:01.532 --> 00:02:03.763
the advice people solicit from you is a

00:02:03.763 --> 00:02:07.057
huge clue as to which of
your skills and expertise

00:02:07.057 --> 00:02:08.795
is most in demand.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.774
And therefore, probably
the most marketable.

00:02:11.774 --> 00:02:13.107
Find your thing.

00:02:21.155 --> 00:02:23.519
(airplane soaring)

